    gas_commitment_bridge: { cell: "R", ev: "SPP-44 (2026-09-07): the SPP leg of this family is the ISO-exclusive row spp_gas_commitment_bridge (its own field, four SPP-measured constants) — screened on 2023 and KILLED at its pre-registered gate (window agreement with CAMPD 0.694 vs 0.76; D-4 unit-conduct FAIL at five laid-up plants); the P0-anchored bridge reaches 0.41 of a 4.2 TWh measured committed-state gap. Same evidence, same verdict: R. FINDING-spp-44-2026-09-07.md. PRIOR: SPP-21 seed U (no verdict minted). SPP-46 (2026-09-07): the family's online-hours leg refused for SPP at zero LP on the same anchor (see spp_gas_commitment_bridge)." },
    spp_gas_commitment_bridge: { cell: "R", ev: "SPP-44 (2026-09-07, ONE rule-29(a) SCREEN on 2023 + its LIVE-hunk control, both deleted before the PR; NO span spent, nothing registered, keeper UNCHANGED keeper-2; PRECOMMIT-spp-44-2026-09-07.md pushed before any solve, FINDING-spp-44-2026-09-07.md): R — KILLED at the pre-registered STOP gate on legs (i) and (iii). The mechanism FIRED as built (7,091 unit-hours, 0.414 TWh of floor, 1,019 segments none > 24 h, D-2 forced share 0.5 % on both classes) but (i) its CC floor lands on plants CAMPD has online at 0.694 against an unconditional 0.660 (lift +0.034, bar 0.76) while ST_GAS agrees at 0.968; (iii) the D-4 unit-conduct check FAILS at five floored plants whose own meter is at zero 53-95 % of the year (CC 201 / 3604 / 8000 / 55178, ST 3485 — the nyiso-144/152 lay-up membership class). Legs (ii) and (iv) pass (dE(CC+ST) +0.180 TWh inside [0.25 V, 2 V]; CT -0.044 = the pre-declared 'CT not displaced'; no non-target flip; C4 r 0.966 / 0.951). THE STRUCTURAL READING: a bridge can only refuse to STOP a unit the model started, and SPP's gas split is units the model never starts — the measured committed-state gap is 4.2 TWh (ST_GAS-carried, 5,914 h at zero in the keeper) and the P0-anchored floor reaches 0.41 TWh of it, with 62 % / 78 % of the CC / ST P0 runs dropped as phantom by the commitment-real screen; the displaced energy is coal (-0.124), not CT. Four MEASURED constants (plant basis 0.209 / 0.090; min-run 15 / 5 h), LOYO-stable to +-0.013; zero tuned. Field landed default-off, seven keeper keys unmoved. Re-test condition: a MEASURED commitment-state membership on the ST_GAS fleet (R-17 (b)) under its own PRECOMMIT — never this leg re-armed on the P0 pattern. SPP-46 (2026-09-07, zero LP): the ONLINE-HOURS state-floor leg (ercot141 / nyiso-146b, R-17 object (b)) was adjudicated on this same P0 anchor and KILLED on reach — it widens the window of the same P0 runs SPP-44 measured 62–78 % phantom, and its reach is bounded by the committed-state footprint in hours the class is on at all: <= 1,977 / 286 / 931 GWh (2023–2025, a class-level over-bound) against ST_GAS under-runs of 8.0 / 5.1 / 7.9 TWh. The MEASURED-state form (CAMPD online hours as the window) fails rule 13's forward test — an observed commitment outcome, not an availability event — and is inadmissible. PRECOMMIT-spp-46 §4.1." },
    reliability_floor: { cell: "U", ev: "SPP-21 (2026-09-06) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/spp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row SPP-21) — U: UNTESTED. SPP has no keeper, no solve and no measurement on this mechanism; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.7." },
