    mustrun_window_commitment_grain: { cell: "K", ev: "PROMOTED 2026-09-11 BY OWNER RULING (verbatim: 'Is this a recommended keeper candidate? If so plz promote. If structural integrity improves but gates regress that may still be a keeper.') \u2014 K: the arm is ARMED ON SPP's DESIGNATED KEEPER, the registered run 2026-09-10-spp-27-commitment-grain (lane SPP-27, docs/RESULT-spp27-span.md; charter docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-spp-27-commitment-grain-2026-09-10.md, screen docs/RESULT-spp27-screen-2023.md), (ninth SPP keeper, over keeper 8 / lane SPP-64). The lane REGISTERED WITHOUT PROMOTING and recommended promotion; the owner then RULED to promote in-session and this cell moved O -> K. THE OBJECT is card R-be, the named rule-17 [R-FLOOR-WINDOW] defect keeper 8 carries. DRIVER, measured from SPP's own CAMPD record at zero LP (22 ST_GAS plants x 3 years): the peak-to-mean of each plant's ONLINE hour-of-day profile is 1.007-1.146 on 21 of 22 (only Mooreland 3008 at 1.609 genuinely two-shifts) and the night/afternoon share of online hours is 0.78-1.09 on 19 of 22 \u2014 when these units are synchronized they run through the overnight trough. Against that, the incumbent hour-ranked window carries the diurnal shape of LOAD (mechanism-level floored-MWh-weighted peak-to-mean 1.235 / 1.216 / 1.216) and implies 2,843 / 3,002 / 2,792 STARTS per year against the meter's 647 / 746 / 778 \u2014 3.65x fleet-wide, 202 starts on 989 MW Muskogee in 2024 against 27 measured. Rule 18 [R-PHYSICS]: a gas-steam unit cannot start 200 times a year. ARMED: window peak-to-mean 1.0000 in all three years by construction and implied starts 288 / 342 / 315, i.e. FEWER than the meter records \u2014 a conservative commitment scaffold. Rule 21 [R-DOF]: ZERO free parameters (no threshold, share, multiplier or length; the grain is the operating day), ledger inherited at n_entries 3 / n_residual 2. Rule 13 [R-MEASURED]: nothing measured enters the PLACEMENT (the ranking is the model's own load shape), so unlike mustrun_online_frac_per_year the field is NOT registered backcast-only. Rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH]: window PLACEMENT alone moves \u2014 SIZE, LEVEL, MEMBERSHIP and hour-eligibility untouched and their four gates all off; the COAL and CT_PEAKER seams deliberately keep the hour grain. SCREEN (2023, named on the mechanism's own largest measured footprint \u2014 858,999.2 MWh moved, 22.20 %, against 19.61 / 19.25 % \u2014 and demonstrably NOT the residual year): SIX of six pre-registered STRUCTURAL STOP gates PASS, none reading the target. SPAN (ONE --years 2023 2024 2025 invocation, 499 s, control = keeper 8's COMMITTED bundle differenced, no control solve, G-DRIFT returned ZERO solve-path files changed): EXACTLY ONE differing scenario_config key across the whole config; offer_curve_by_group byte-identical; dump 0 and slack byte-identical to the keeper (0 / 370.1017 / 0 MWh); system price max byte-identical (59.3126 / 2000.0000 / 73.7731) so C3c cannot and does not move. SCORED IDENTICAL TO THE KEEPER on every criterion, re-scored live at HEAD rubric v3.7: CALIBRATED, grade 7 of 8, 0 fails, 1 ledgered C3c caveat, free-class C1 16/16 all / 12/12 free, C1/C2/C3a/C3b/C4/C6/C8 all PASS. ST_GAS gross +0.2801 / +0.2004 / +0.2403 TWh paid by coal and CC_REGULAR, wind -0.011 %; C5a within 0.1 pp; C8 forced share 0.2112 / 0.1969 / 0.1825 against a 0.30 cap. THE ADVERSE FINDING, REPORTED NOT ABSORBED: the arm does NOT close R-be. D4.passed stays False and the conduct-FAIL count is 4 / 4 / 4 against the keeper's 4 / 5 / 3 \u2014 the SAME TOTAL OF 12. It removes 1230 in 2024 (zero_share 0.5906 -> 0.4408, PASS) and improves 1230 / 1235 / 1271 in 2023 (0.7018 -> 0.6096, 0.6230 -> 0.5606, 0.6976 -> 0.5875) without crossing the bar, and it ADDS Mooreland 3008 in 2025 (0.4735 -> 0.5262) \u2014 the one measured two-shifter, for which a uniform whole-day window is the wrong grain. Mooreland is NOT special-cased: a per-plant grain predicate needs a threshold (rule 21) and choosing it against this statistic is the fitted-mechanism selection rule 1 [R-STRUCT](c) forbids; a plant exclusion is refused on miso-170's warning that it 'would bury that error inside a membership list'. The residual R-be is day SELECTION (for 1230/1235/1271 the day-selection lift over chance is only ~2x and no forecast-admissible signal reaches it) plus a SIZE component that is NOT a defect (pooled online_frac is the rule-13-admissible construction and necessarily mis-sizes an individual year; mustrun_online_frac_per_year is REFUSED here as backcast-only). VARIANTS MEASURED AND DELIBERATELY NOT TAKEN, declared so the choice is not hidden: a day-PEAK key and a NET-load signal score marginally better on the conduct-overlap statistic (0.8368 vs 0.8238 over 65 plant-years) and were refused because each bundles a second, independently-unmotivated change \u2014 net-vs-gross is a WASH at the hour grain. Nothing was swept against any gate. DO-NOT-REDO: do not re-test the day-peak or net-load variants without new driver evidence, and do not reach for mustrun_plant_exclusions on Mooreland. SPP-39 ANNOTATION 2026-09-13 (rule 28(b) duty; NO VERDICT MINTED and this cell KEEPS its K -- nothing was tested, only MEASURED at zero LP off keeper 11's committed artifacts). Card R-be's remaining DAY-SELECTION half was expected by the SPP prompt pack to CLOSE at phase 0 on 'no forecast-admissible signal reaches it'. IT DOES NOT CLOSE. (1) The object SHRANK: the SPP-38 vintage-cache repair resolved 2 of keeper 10's 12 failing D-4 rows -- (2024, plant 6193) and (2025, plant 1230), new-failure set EMPTY -- so the card is now 10 rows on 4 plants. 6193 is HARRINGTON, the coal-to-gas conversion that was the largest term in the stale vintage map, so its D-4 failure was an artifact of the leak. (2) THE SIZE HYPOTHESIS IS REFUTED: an ORACLE ranking (days by the plant's OWN measured online hours -- the best any selection rule could do) clears the 0.50 bar on 10 of 10 rows, margins 0.00-0.35, so the window is NOT size-bound and day selection is the right object. (3) THE ADMISSIBLE SET IS NOT EMPTY: day-mean gross (incumbent), day-PEAK gross, day-mean NET and day-peak net are all rule-13 admissible (each is the MODEL'S OWN array, regenerated forward by construction); only temperature/weather and an SPP commitment or outage instrument are unreachable (no committed weather driver; LTLF and audit items 15/16/19 blocked). PAIRED measurement, same instrument both arms so the bias cancels: day-mean NET load beats the incumbent on 7 of 10 rows, mean -0.0335; day-PEAK gross is WORSE. (4) BOUNDED HONESTLY: the reconstruction does NOT reproduce the scorer (two tried; the per-plant floors collapse reproduces 0 of 10 because the rider scores per class-SLICE), so the PAIRED SIGN survives and any absolute 0.50-crossing claim does NOT -- an earlier pass's '5 of 10 clear 0.50' is WITHDRAWN. (5) NOT PROMOTABLE: SPP-27 refused NET load at the HOUR grain as a WASH (0.8168 vs 0.8168); this is the DAY grain, which is new evidence under rule 28(a), but A STATISTIC IS NOT A DRIVER and adopting it because it scores better on the rider it is scored against is the fitted-mechanism selection rule 1 [R-STRUCT](c) forbids. Successor (spp-40, ZERO LP): make the D-4 rider reproducible per class-slice, then re-run the comparison on a faithful instrument; a PRECOMMIT only if net load still wins AND a driver argument lands from SPP's own commitment record. docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-39-day-selection-2026-09-13.md." },
