    unit_outage_short_windows_gas: { cell: "R", ev: "Row added by pjm-d4-4 (2026-09-10) with the field, same PR (rule 28c). UNTESTED here (rule 28(d)): a verdict is strictly per-ISO and PJM\u0027s does not fill this cell \u2014 no parameter transfers, since the scope carries none. The transfer question is cheap, zero-LP and well-posed: derive this ISO\u0027s own gas sub-5-day family (--short-windows --short-window-groups gas --merit-order-guard), measure its annual-mean and event-hour MW against this ISO\u0027s own published forced/planned composition gap, and check the per-stratum correlation sign against this ISO\u0027s own published FORCED series before proposing anything. An ISO whose gas fleet is small, or whose published record is not typed, may find the family immaterial or the identification unavailable. MOVED U -> R by SPP-32 (2026-09-12): REJECTED for SPP on two pre-registered gates, and this is a rule 28(d) NON-TRANSFER demonstrated rather than asserted. SPP had no gas extract, so one was derived from SPP's OWN CAMPD record with an invocation BYTE-IDENTICAL to PJM's committed sidecar on every knob (fullstop_override_cf 0.02, fullstop_override_days 5, high_load_pctl 0.85, min_inmerit_hours 6, min_outage_days 1.0, merit_order_guard true; only iso and years differ) -- data/raw/campd-unit-outages-shortgas-SPP.csv, 2,838 windows, 39 plants, 75 units, CC_REGULAR 2,204 / ST_GAS 608 / CC_CHP 26. Zero parameters chosen by the lane, nothing swept. Nested by construction: data/fleet/arrays.py opens the block on unit_outage_short_windows and passes gas_scope inside it, so the gas flag is inert alone and the arm carries BOTH. Screen year 2025 (largest measured footprint, 11,354.227 GWh / 1,063 windows against 2024's 9,297.096 / 840 and 2023's 10,762.570 / 935). MEASURED, one shard, 138 s: the overlay fires at 218 plant-tranches, and the shard's own zero-LP probe of unit_outage_short_derate_factors confirms the gas scope really entered -- 23 plant-groups at gas_scope False vs 55 at True (COAL 23 + CC_REGULAR 18 + ST_GAS 13 + CC_CHP 1), coal unchanged either way. G1/G2/G3 clear (confinement exact; response 3.8175 TWh inside its 9.43 TWh bound). THE KILL: G4 identity FAILS at slack 10,911.0219 MWh in 12 hours, ALL in SPP-South, in three clusters (2025-09-15, 2025-10-06, 2025-12-21), every hour at VOLL $2,000; and G5 FLIPS BOTH load-bearing price criteria PASS -> FAIL (C3a 28.7893 -> 33.1683 = +15.97 % against a +/-10 % band; C3b 0.1638 -> 0.2619 against a 0.20 bar). The entire price move is scarcity, not merit order -- all 18 hours above $200 are exactly $2,000, the slack penalty -- so the arm does not price SPP better, it makes SPP infeasible. THE FAILURE MODE WAS PRE-REGISTERED: PRECOMMIT section 7 named it before the solve ('2,838 gas windows over three years is too many for a merit-order guard to have filtered -- SPP's CC fleet runs at ~49 % CF, and a 1-5 day dead span at that CF can be economics rather than an outage'). PJM's and MISO's K on the coal parent do not carry here and the reason is fleet conduct, not plumbing. THE EXTRACT STAYS COMMITTED -- what is rejected is arming it in SPP's LP, not the data. Evidence: docs/RESULT-spp-32-shortwindow-screen-2026-09-12.md, docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-spp-32-shortwindow-availability-2026-09-12.md, docs/handoffs/SHARDREPORT-spp32-B-2025.md." },
