    unit_outage_window_hour_grain: { cell: "U", ev: "Row added by nyiso-229 (2026-09-12) with the field, same PR (rule 28c). UNTESTED here (rule 28(d)): the defect\u0027s SIZE is a per-ISO data property \u2014 how much of each ISO\u0027s day-grain window mass sits at a boundary the detector never detected \u2014 so NYISO\u0027s measurement fills NYISO\u0027s cell only, and a lane adopting it derives its OWN \u0027-perunitmerithour-\u0027 extract from its own CAMPD (no number crosses). The three-step protocol is zero-LP and is NYISO\u0027s, reusable verbatim: (1) count the unit-hours the loader asserts unavailable while the meter shows grossLoad > 0, and split them by distance from the nearest window boundary \u2014 within 23 h is SCHEMA rounding, deeper is DETECTOR misplacement and a different defect; (2) count same-unit day-grain window overlaps and check the histogram is a single 24.0 h bin (the shared-boundary-day fingerprint); (3) check the ISO has tight hours for the restored capacity to reach \u2014 firm-load slack OR a short reserve family \u2014 because a lever that gives capacity back to a market with slack everywhere is inert. Predicated on campd_per_unit_attribution AND campd_outage_merit_order_guard, so an ISO arming neither reads the field as n/a in practice." },
