    coal_passthrough_sigmoids: { cell: "I", ev: "SPP-41 (2026-09-14) CONSTRUCTION OBSERVATION, ZERO LP — I: keeper 11's ARMED coal_prb_passthrough_sigmoid + coal_prb_passthrough_tiered are PROVABLY INERT for SPP, so run_config.json/meta.json OVERSTATE what the solve read (rule 24 [R-REGISTRY]; the xiso-3 armed-looking-but-dead shape). COAL_SIGMOID_DEFAULTS carries 10 entries across ERCOT/MISO/PJM and NO ('SPP', *) key; keeper 11 leaves all four coal_prb_passthrough_* scalars None; so fuel.trajectories.coal_sigmoid_params returns None for EVERY supply and coal_passthrough_series returns the FLAT coal_prb_passthrough = 1.0. MEASURED in the arrays rather than read off the source, via four run_year(fleet_only=True) rebuilds of keeper 11's own recipe: the implied PRB econ passthrough (mc - vom)/(fuel x heat_rate), with the 0.93 band multiplier already baked into fleet_arrays.heat_rate, reads EXACTLY 1.00000 at p05/p50/p95 over 46 plants in all four of 2024/2023/2021/2022 — gas-INVARIANT across $2.19-$6.45, a 3x range. A live sigmoid would move it (ERCOT's registered PRB curve runs 0.78 -> 1.50 about gas_mid 2.85). ROOT CAUSE: SPP is absent from data/raw/reference/coal_region_crosswalk.csv (ISOs CAISO/ERCOT/MISO/NEISO/PJM), which derive_coal_sigmoid.py iterates, so no SPP row exists in coal_sigmoid_params.csv either — SPP was onboarded without the coal-supply-chain derivation every other coal ISO has (coal_supply_SPP.csv DOES exist; it is the REGION crosswalk that is missing). THE OBVIOUS REPAIR IS DEAD AND WAS KILLED AT ZERO LP: derive_coal_sigmoid.py fixes ceil = 1.0 for every supply by design (its header, 'retires the inconsistent ceil>1.0 opportunity-cost story the D-8 audit flagged'), and all 10 derived rows carry ceil 1.0; applied to SPP at either existing PRB shape the merit-order position (share of CC econ MW above the PRB econ median, hour by hour) moves 95.0 -> 95.7 % in 2021 and 96.7 -> 96.7 % in 2022 (EXACTLY inert in the two FAILING years, since passthrough -> 1.000 at $6.45 which is what the model already does) while 2023 goes 39.5 -> 97.3 % (ERCOT shape) / 87.4 % (MISO shape), i.e. it would destroy both CALIBRATED years. NOT re-opened without a different functional form. Evidence: docs/handoffs/RESULT-spp-41-coal-gas-crossover-2026-09-14.md §2.1-§2.3, scripts/probes/_spp41_crossover_phase0.py + _spp41_passthrough_and_crossing.py. No cell in any other ISO is touched (rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d))." },
