    negative_renewable_offers: { cell: "I", ev: "SPP-51b (2026-09-09, ZERO LP; docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-spp-51b-2026-09-08.md leg C, FINDING-spp-51b-2026-09-09.md §4) — U -> I: INERT on the wind limb, rule-25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] REFUSED on the solar limb. Measured on six on-recipe fleet_only rebuilds of keeper-3 at HEAD: SPP wind's dispatch offer is ALREADY -$26.000/MWh in all three years (the full §45 PTC via compute_dispatch_credits, ira_ptc_wind = 26.0), so this flag's floor min(-26, -renewable_keep_running_value = -20) IS -26 and changes nothing — the flag is a no-op on the only curtailable column that matters in SPP. The solar limb would put SPP solar at -$20, which the field's own docstring adjudicates as CAISO's RPS/REC keep-running value and forbids re-using on another ISO (the same ERCOT-65 scoping). NOT a statement that negative prices are unreachable — the OPPOSITE: in the 7 / 7 / 3 hours per year where the LP holds wind strictly inside its bound, the zonal price is EXACTLY -$26.00 in every one, and the whole-year minimum zonal price is -$26.00 in all three years. The price-formation path is correct, complete and already armed; what is missing is the QUANTITY of wind potential in the oversupply hours (the flat delivered/(1-0.096501) gross-up, verified flat to 99.94/99.93/99.98% of hours, spreads SPP's measured 9.65% curtailment uniformly instead of onto the ~1,000 hours where it happened). SPP's object is that allocation, routed as SPP-51b R-1, not this bid flag." },
    wind_ptc_vintage_offers: { cell: "I", ev: "SPP-51b (2026-09-09, ZERO LP; PRECOMMIT-spp-51b leg C-2, FINDING-spp-51b §4) — U -> I: INERT, and for a reason that outlives the verdict. (i) DIRECTION: scoping the offer to in-window vintages can only make wind's bid LESS negative than the flat -$26.000/MWh measured on keeper-3's arrays at HEAD, i.e. the wrong way for SPP's object (a missing sub-$0 regime, FINDING §0.1). (ii) REACH: a bid change on a column that is never marginal cannot move a price — SPP wind sits AT its upper bound in 99.92 / 99.92 / 99.97 % of hours (interior in 7 / 7 / 3 of 8,760; LP re-curtailment 0.00248 / 0.00184 / 0.00043 % against SPP's measured 9.65 %). Both legs measured, neither inferred, no LP spent and no other ISO's verdict consulted (rules 25 / 28(d)). Re-openable only if SPP's wind ever becomes materially marginal, i.e. after the SPP-51b R-1 allocation object lands." },
    gas_offer_curve_tranches: { cell: "U", ev: "SPP-21 (2026-09-06) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/spp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row SPP-21) — U: UNTESTED. SPP has no keeper, no solve and no measurement on this mechanism; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.7." },
    gas_electric_power_monthly_level: { cell: "U", ev: "MINTED U by the rule-28(c) same-PR duty only (xiso-fuelvintage-1, 2026-09-09) \u2014 NO SPP adjudication made or implied; SPP was explicitly out of this session's scope. For the record the phase-0 measurement puts SPP with MISO as the two ISOs still on the generic climatological shape in every year (model monthly CV 0.094 throughout), admissible 2022-2024 with a Jan-2022 gap of 13.368 $/MMBtu (~100 $/MWh); 2019-2021 and 2025 inert because Oklahoma (37.5% of SPP gas capacity) prints no N3045 month." },
    gas_monthly_actuals: { cell: "U", ev: "SPP PRICE-FAMILY (2026-09-07) — STILL U: NOT ARMED, no verdict minted. Recorded because the zero-LP decomposition ANSWERED a rule-14 question negatively for the C3a/C3b residual specifically: SPP's measured price surface does NOT follow gas (corr(monthly actual price, KS/OK delivered gas) = +0.2720) while the MODEL's already does (+0.6969), and the market heat rate is not constant (CV 0.3874) — SPP INVERTS PJM (0.9531 / 0.2449 / 0.082). Price follows LOAD (+0.7791). So a richer gas series cannot be the C3a/C3b cause. It remains a live measured-input question in its own right (this run prices gas off a flat annual scalar 2.54/2.19/3.52 with gas_plant_monthly_fuel_pricing True, and data/raw/spp_zonal_gas_hub.csv exists unarmed) and was NOT tested as an arm. docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-price-family-2026-09-07.md §1." },
    gas_plant_monthly_pricing: { cell: "K", ev: "SPP-21 (2026-09-06) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/spp-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row SPP-21) — U: UNTESTED. SPP has no keeper, no solve and no measurement on this mechanism; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.7. CORRECTED SPP-46 (2026-09-07): the seed line above is STALE — keeper-3's recipe ARMS this mechanism (run_config: gas_plant_monthly_fuel_pricing=True, nearby_fuel_price_fallback=True, min_state_plants 2, class-aware off; 383 / 383 / 343 gas rows priced from their own plant, 792 / 792 / 820 from the zone pool — every SPP row's state is empty so the state tiers are void), so the cell reads K by the keeper it is in. MEASURED AT ZERO LP (PRECOMMIT-spp-46 §3, FINDING-spp-46): the seam has NO plausibility screen and the SPP-state EIA-923 gas frame carries 91 plant-months <= $0.50, 31 NEGATIVE and 206 >= $10 of 5,707 (2023–2025); keeper-3 consumes them at face value and they carry the C1-2024 gas split (own-priced rows: CT fuel_low +8.1 TWh, ST_GAS fuel_high -3.8, Harrington $1.48 +5.8; clean CT -0.24). Re-clearing keeper-3's cleared quantity with a declared [0.5, 2.0] x state-reference (N3045<ST>3) own-month screen predicts 2024 CC +4.3 / CT -4.2 / COAL +4.0 / ST -4.2 (Harrington) at a +3.2 % level. The screen is a rule-14 zero-DOF repair on a shared seam (data/fuel/plant_prices.py) and is ROUTED (SPP-46 R-1), not built by the lane." },
