    vre_curtailment_oversupply_allocation: { cell: "K", ev: "SPP-51c (2026-09-09): BUILT IT, SCREENED IT, THE PRE-REGISTERED STRUCTURAL GATE KILLED IT, AND THE OWNER PROMOTED IT ANYWAY -- cell K, ARMED IN THE SPP KEEPER 2026-09-09-spp-51c-oversupply-curtailment. The R -> K move is an OWNER RULING, in session, verbatim: 'Is this a recommended keeper candidate? If so plz promote. If structural integrity improves but gates regress that may still be a keeper.' The session had recommended AGAINST promotion on the failed gate and that recommendation is NOT withdrawn, re-cut or re-scored. PRECOMMIT-spp-51c-2026-09-09.md + ADDENDUM pushed before any number was read / before the screen ran; FINDING-spp-51c-2026-09-09.md. THE MECHANISM: it re-allocates the HOURS of SPP's measured wind curtailment and changes NO annual total -- annual potential 114.0552/120.9925/122.2552 TWh, IDENTICAL to the flat rule's in every year, so rule 23 [R-FROZEN-DERIVE] is untouched -- by water-filling the frozen energy onto the lowest-net-load hours at the level lambda (16.15/16.48/17.58 GW) that makes the annual identity hold. ZERO new free parameters; DOF ledger UNCHANGED at 3 entries / 1 residual. WHAT IT DELIVERS, all three runs RE-SCORED on the same repaired bench so this is like-for-like: C1 failing rows keeper-3 TWO / SPP-50 one / THIS one; C3a failing years keeper-3 one (+11.0 %) / SPP-50 TWO (+11.9, +11.6) / THIS one (2025 +10.3); C3b failing years keeper-3 two / SPP-50 THREE / THIS one (2025 0.204). Against its OWN control (SPP-50, identical recipe without the field on the identical inputs) it is BETTER ON EVERY CRITERION and worse on none. It creates SPP's negative-price regime for the first time -- 229/214/159 system load-weighted hours < $0 against a control of essentially zero -- pricing at EXACTLY -$26.00 where wind is marginal, which reproduces SPP-51b's price-formation finding under a live mechanism. Determination NOT-YET, unchanged from keeper-3. WHY THE GATE STILL FAILED, AND IT IS THE TRANSFERABLE RESULT: G-1a predicted 871 interior-wind hours (band 348-2178) and measured 177; G-1b predicted 592 (band 237-1480) and measured 159; G-3 predicted the wind identity in 1.02-1.09 and it moved only 1.10681 -> 1.10489 (LP re-curtailment 0.174 % against a measured 9.65 %). G-2 also failed as written (53.67 % vs 90 %) but was MIS-SPECIFIED by the lane -- it measured against the FLAT bound, which the mechanism moves in every hour by construction; the property it meant to test reads 100.0 % (all 212,240 MWh of re-curtailment inside the 3,025 named hours, zero outside) and is reported as a diagnostic, NEVER as a gate pass. ROOT CAUSE, measured on the arm's own sidecars: the LP ABSORBS 98.2 % of the concentrated headroom by displacing thermal instead of spilling wind -- in the 2,848 allocated 2025 hours where wind did not go interior, thermal averaged 8,454 MW and still had 8,200 MW of turn-down available (2,624 of them with over 2 GW spare), and the model's thermal ANNUAL MINIMUM is 254.3 MW across a ~40 GW fleet because SPP carries ZERO commitment floors and ZERO bridges. So the binding limb is R-2, the thermal-commitment floor, and this is DIRECT MEASURED EVIDENCE AGAINST SPP-51b's own sizing note, which placed the deficit on the wind side. Rule 19 [R-ONE-MECH]: any successor floor must be RECONCILED with this allocation, never stacked on the un-diagnosed residual of the flat rule. ALSO LANDED BY THIS LANE, an input repair and not a model change: the committed SPP actual-LMP sidecar was indexed on SPP's GMT market interval while the model's 8760 calendar is FIXED Central Standard Time, so C3a's hour-matched rt_lw had been scoring against a series SIX HOURS out of phase. Repaired by a pure re-indexing (sorted value set identical, equal-hour annual mean unchanged to four decimals), direction and the constant +6 fixed by physical markers and by SPP's own GMT-stamped GenMix load, never by a residual; a six-ISO census isolates the defect to SPP alone. EVERY SPP C3a/C3b NUMBER OLDER THAN 2026-09-09 IS ON THE UNREPAIRED CLOCK AND IS NOT COMPARABLE." },
    vre_reference_rate_curtailment_grossup: { cell: "U", ev: "SPP-21 (2026-09-06) shard seed, no verdict minted — U: UNTESTED; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. SPP-51b EVIDENCE APPENDED 2026-09-09, STILL U — the mechanism's FOOTPRINT was measured at zero LP but NO ARM WAS SOLVED, so no verdict is minted (rule 28(b)); this is the SPP-54 `measured_interface_limits` precedent. What was measured (FINDING-spp-51b-2026-09-09.md §3, on keeper-3's committed bundle + six fleet_only rebuilds at HEAD): the gross-up SPP is armed with is FLAT — model wind = 1.106808 x delivered_EIA930(t) in 99.94 / 99.93 / 99.98 % of hours — so it preserves the DELIVERED shape, and delivered is already net of curtailment. The measured 9.65 % (SPP-32, both legs measured) is therefore spread uniformly over all 8,760 hours, i.e. everywhere except the ~1,000 hours where curtailment occurred, and the LP re-curtails 0.00248 / 0.00184 / 0.00043 % against renewables.py's own stated design intent ('so the LP still curtails endogenously'). The ENERGY is right and its ALLOCATION is the defect: 11.006 / 11.676 / 11.798 TWh sit in the gross-up against 5.676 / 7.425 / 5.355 TWh needed to make the measured-negative hours long (1.94x / 1.57x / 2.20x). A pre-registered candidate reallocation — potential(t) = max(delivered(t), A_hat x the committed SPP-48 reanalysis fleet shape), annual-potential identity preserved exactly, ZERO new free parameters — was COSTED, not solved: it moves +999 / +1,005 / +2,022 MW into those hours against a 5,721 / 6,335 / 5,260 MW deficit, closing 17.5 / 15.9 / 38.4 %. NECESSARY BUT NOT SUFFICIENT, as the PRECOMMIT predicted against its own interest (leg B-4), because a reanalysis shape predicts wind AVAILABILITY while curtailment is availability meeting low net load and congestion. The successor is an allocation instrument keyed on OVERSUPPLY (SPP-51b R-1); the annual rate is measured and must not be re-derived (rule 23 [R-FROZEN-DERIVE])." },
