    hydro_vintage_input_repair: { cell: "K", ev: "SPP-42 (2026-09-07) — K: KEEPER, armed on 2026-09-07-spp-2-crosswalk-hydro (bundle spp42_crosswalk_B; docs/handoffs/FINDING-spp-42-2026-09-07.md §2-§3). The pair --hydro-backfill-year 2024 --hydro-eia930-monthly, applied to every year (rule 22: a measured input is never held out): the EIA-923 preliminary 2025 vintage carried 0.0233 TWh of SPP hydro (1 plant) against the measured EIA-930 NG:WAT 8.8299 TWh; 21 plants backfilled from 2024 and the monthly level pinned; 2023 / 2024 re-pinned 8.4003 -> 8.3441 / 8.7023 -> 8.9731 TWh. Zero-LP prediction (build_hydro_fleet) reproduced exactly by the solve (8.82 TWh dispatched). Rule-29(a) 2025 screen: unserved 2,007 MWh in 6 h -> 89.3 MWh in 1 h (100 % of the North cleared, 91 % of the South); the charter gate's literal unserved->0 leg NOT met and the lane proceeded on rule 14 (stated, FINDING §2.3). Differenced against the spp-1 control: C3a-2025 +21.7 % -> +7.2 %, C3b-2025 0.283 -> 0.189, coal/CC/CT/ST 2025 -2.4 / -2.0 / -2.7 / -1.7 TWh. A rule-14 INPUT correction with zero free parameters, not a lever. Also found by this lane and ROUTED (P9): EIA-930 SWPP Demand carries stuck identical-value runs (2025: 698 h in 19 runs, longest 155 h from 2025-12-15; 2024: 396 h; 2023: 36 h) that the 2.5x spike screen cannot see." },
